course: dictionary
lesson: 7223
title: Photograph: a picture or an action
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A photograph can be a noun or a verb, so check how it is used in the sentence. As a noun, it is the picture itself: «Clyde Tombaugh found Pluto by comparing photographs of the sky taken days apart.» Here photographs are pictures, and you could hold them in an album.
explain: As a verb, to photograph something means to take a picture of it with a camera. «Photographing children and animals from their eye level makes the picture feel closer and more natural.» Someone is doing the action, so this is the verb form.
explain: Use the context to decide. Ask: is this a thing I could hold, or is someone doing something? Then swap in the meaning «a picture made with a camera» or «take a picture of it with a camera» and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A photograph is a picture made with a camera.
fact: To photograph something is to take a picture of it with a camera.
fact: «Photographs» is the plural noun, and «photographing» is the verb form used while the action is happening.
fact: Useful phrases: take a photograph, school photograph, photograph album.
fact: Online safety: ask before photographing someone, and do not share photographs of yourself with strangers.
exercise: «Pluto was discovered in 1930 by comparing photographs of the sky taken days apart.» What are photographs here? | *Pictures made with a camera | Sounds recorded by a microphone | Telescopes that find planets | Stars that move across the night
exercise: Mia wants to take a picture of her dog with her camera. Which word means this? | whisper | *photograph | sketch | measure
exercise: «Photographing children and animals from their eye level makes the picture feel closer and more natural.» Find and copy the verb form. | eye | children | closer | *Photographing
test: Before you photograph a friend at school, what should you do? | *Ask them first | Hide the camera behind a bag | Take the picture from far away so they will not notice | Post the picture online straight away
test: Which of these is a photograph? | A song played on the radio | A drawing of a horse done in pencil | A map of the town with roads marked | *A picture of your holiday taken with a camera
exam: Which sentence uses photograph as a verb? | The photograph album is on the top shelf. | Lara holds a photograph of her gran in her hand. | *Lara will photograph the science experiment to record her results. | The photograph was taken last summer at the seaside.
